@startuml
title Student Feature — Component Diagram (Specify)
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor Student
component "Student Web Experience\nJoin / Activity / Answers / Results" as StudentUI
component "Student Feature Services\nIdentity · Enrollment · Team Choice\nShared Draft · Submission · Result View" as StudentServices
component "Shared Foundation\nSession · Round · Target · State" as Foundation
component "Shared Data Model\nParticipant · Team · Submission\nSubmissionAnswer · Result" as SharedData
component "Teacher Feature\nActivity / Teams / Targets / Lifecycle" as Teacher
cloud "Connected clients\nSession state notifications" as Realtime

Student --> StudentUI
StudentUI --> StudentServices : student actions
StudentServices --> Foundation : verified reads / shared lifecycle data
StudentServices --> SharedData : student-owned membership and submissions
Foundation --> SharedData : shared concepts and persistence boundary
Teacher --> Foundation : provides activity targets and lifecycle
Foundation --> Realtime : phase snapshots
Realtime --> StudentUI : current state and changes
Teacher --> SharedData : prepares activity data

note bottom of StudentServices
Participant identity is activity-scoped, passwordless,
and recoverable in the same browser; credential mechanics
remain for Plan. Student Feature persists and immediately
shares team drafts; accepted submission makes the draft
read-only. Student Feature selects the first accepted submission
and provides the student result projection. Teacher calls the
trusted resolver before Foundation's existing End transaction;
coordinate that internal boundary with Teacher Feature. Do not
extend Foundation state events or public contracts with answers.
If the leader cannot return, authorized Teacher transfer
requires coordination with Teacher Feature.
Student-supplied role, Team ID and acceptedOrder
are never authoritative.
end note

note bottom of Foundation
Reuse existing shared routes, read contracts,
ActorContext boundary and Socket.IO state contract.
Do not change Foundation contracts in Specify.
end note
@enduml
